  "description": [
    {
      "value": "<p>A stopped reed just over a metre long with four finger holes and a sliding collar, blown to carry the prosody of terrace speech between levels rather than to make music. A competent player reproduces a sentence closely enough that the answer comes back in words, and it is the collar that does the work; the holes are for the vowels. This is a working instrument from the water corporation, taken out of use when the terrace it served was cleared. Visitors transcribed the surrogate as music for eleven years, and those transcriptions are in the archive, filed under music.</p>",
      "inLanguage": [{ "id": ["core.peerdb.org", "LANGUAGE", "en-GB"] }]
    }
  ],
